  <title>Circles and ellipses</title>

  <p><gui>+ Circle</gui> adds a circle and <gui>+ Ellipse</gui> an
  ellipse.</p>

  <terms>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Diameter</gui></title>
      <p>A circle's size in dots, 3 to 4095. A circle always stays round:
      dragging any handle changes its diameter.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Width</gui> and <gui>Height</gui></title>
      <p>An ellipse's size in dots, 3 to 4095 each, set freely.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Thickness</gui></title>
      <p>The ring, drawn inward from the outline. At the radius (half the
      shorter side, for an ellipse) the shape is solid black.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title><gui>Colour</gui> and <gui>Reverse</gui></title>
      <p>As for a <link xref="frame">frame</link>: white prints only over
      something black, and <gui>Reverse</gui> turns what is beneath the ring
      white.</p>
    </item>
  </terms>
</page>
